  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# Changelog 0.0.769\n\n## Changes since v0.0.662\n\n- Standalone: single-file publishes self-extract so the macOS package builds again (#1221) (`baeadc4a`)\n- Portable2D: Random draws reserve no RAM of their own (#1220) (`6608d990`)\n- A word comparison evaluates each computed operand once (#1203) (#1219) (`112677bd`)\n- Language server and Claude Code plugin: retrosharp lsp, retrosharp check (#1218) (`958303d9`)\n- Portable2D: deterministic Random source (#1199) (#1217) (`e3ba09ca`)\n- Portable2D: World.Strip composes a scrolling world from borders and fill for any screen width (#1214) (#1215) (`a91b7592`)\n- Portable2D: World.RepeatVertically scrolls a repeating world without end (#1198) (#1213) (`5a97eb95`)\n- Stop tracking generated ROMs; tests compile what they check (#1207) (#1212) (`bd66df9e`)\n- Use the renamed Zafiro debugger packages (#1211) (`386b9c74`)\n- Runtime multiplication, division, remainder and shifts on every target (#1197) (#1209) (`124853ee`)\n- Shorter test suite: faster banked compiles, long classes first, fewer repeated compiles (#1201) (#1208) (`6a286c7e`)\n- Samples and generated actor/projectile code test camera AABB overlap as bool (#1202) (`235ec0f4`)\n- GB camera publishes its scroll before streaming the edge (#1046) (#1195) (`bd88c39b`)\n- Word assignments read the destination before overwriting it (#1194) (`52ef9327`)\n- Camera AABB overlap answers bool (#1192) (`cea7ecf8`)\n- Relational conditions branch directly when the jump is taken on true (#1191) (`b793d1a3`)\n- Sprites: pieces past a screen edge no longer show on the other side (#1185) (`63a936a8`)\n- push-box builds for the Game Gear with the Game Boy layout (#1172) (`6bf32c04`)\n- snow-bros-jr builds for the Game Gear (#1171) (`a613d89f`)\n- runner and runner-lift build for the Game Gear (#1170) (`c27d6bf4`)\n- Game Gear: the camera scrolls and streams inside the 160x144 window (#1175) (`39991add`)\n- Game Gear builds as a profile of the Master System target (#1169) (`3bccbe40`)\n- Master System: actor pools draw actors left of the camera with a signed X (#1167) (`25a9666a`)\n- snow-bros-jr builds for the Master System (#1141) (`63ad532a`)\n- Master System: streamed sprite tiles take the room of an unwritten camera edge (#1155) (`5c217d23`)\n- push-box builds for the Master System (#1142) (`88e54ba2`)\n- Master System: sprite asset tiles as background (#1152) (`a73e0e69`)\n- Master System: runtime Tilemap.Set queued for VBlank (#1151) (`05f56682`)\n- Master System: stream sprite tiles past the pattern table (#1149) (`14abddd3`)\n- Master System: wider frame margin for runner-lift (#1146) (`050d37c7`)\n- Master System: border and blanked left column show the world's background color (#1145) (`48879ce4`)\n- Master System: explicit layout form of Sprite.Asset (#1148) (`1302115c`)\n- Master System: runner-lift as an acceptance game; byte-cast sprite coordinates; Camera.Init leaves scroll registers to Apply (#1140) (`57543e47`)\n- Master System: runner as an acceptance game (#1139) (`ec87754d`)\n- Master System: actors reset on world activation; world-activation sample (#1134) (`9684da7a`)\n- Master System: Animation.Clip/Frame through the shared Z80 lookup, actor pool budgets and actor samples (#1133) (`513d8d1d`)\n- Master System: sprite art falls back to NES then Game Boy variants; platform samples with acceptance (#1132) (`abea82a8`)\n- Screen collision queries answer the rows the screen shows over a band world (#1124) (`c2e09761`)\n- Master System: Tiled background tile animation and BackgroundAnimation.SetEnabled (#1119) (`a48c1ae1`)\n- Master System: audio samples with functional scenarios (#1097) (`172ced12`)\n- Master System: Button.Select reads as never held with a warning, and managed-audio (#1121) (`75e0dc5f`)\n- Master System: music-switch from DMG VGM logs beside its Game Boy songs (#1113) (`154ad8df`)\n- Master System: functional audio service and progress evidence (#1112) (`11c0204a`)\n- Master System: shots samples and projectile acceptance; shots-bouncy floor on screen (#1034) (`485b06bf`)\n- Master System: Camera.Follow, Sprite.DrawWorld and actor camera reads (#1107) (`d91fc4c1`)\n- Master System: logical palettes Palette.Background and Palette.Sprite (#1111) (`b6730058`)\n- Master System: world activation over WorldAsset worlds (#1106) (`b407eebf`)\n- Master System: large worlds split across banks, and tiled-tall (#1105) (`a8099212`)\n- Master System: World.Load Tiled worlds through the raw route (#1104) (`15328a59`)\n- Master System: AABB collision over World.Map and World.Flags (#1103) (`9b38a421`)\n- Master System: sprite flips through mirrored copies and cross-target-camera acceptance (#1101) (`87e77b5e`)\n- Master System: read-only data in switchable Sega mapper banks (#1098) (#1110) (`1c929564`)\n- Master System: transcode NES 2A03 and Game Boy DMG VGM logs to the PSG (#1096) (#1109) (`b44721a9`)\n- Master System: SN76489 PSG player for music and sound effects (#1095) (#1108) (`36af5b15`)\n- Master System: camera and hardware scrolling over World.Map worlds (#1033) (#1102) (`f0f437d1`)\n- Master System: Sprite.Draw through the SAT and the cross-target sprite-draw sample (#1093) (#1100) (`791f10bb`)\n- Master System: Sega mapper program banking (#1036) (#1099) (`199e8ad3`)\n- Master System: 4bpp sprite assets and the sprite palette from the neutral plan (#1092) (#1094) (`a6d83f5a`)\n- Master System: portable input on the two-button pad and Pause as Start (#1031) (#1091) (`e0aaedf5`)\n- Master System: static drawing through the VDP and the static-drawing sample (#1088) (#1090) (`d1bb2b95`)\n- Master System: minimal ROM compiler with boot, VDP init and frame loop (#1087) (#1089) (`16d93047`)\n- Z80 family: move the language core into RetroSharp.Z80Family (#1084) (#1086) (`0f3f3d24`)\n- Z80 family: language core as its own class with explicit dependencies (#1083) (#1085) (`63c4f442`)\n- Z80 family: storage layout for the language core (#1076) (#1082) (`f0f395bf`)\n- Z80 family: target lowering port for the language core (#1075) (#1081) (`717eba82`)\n- NES: sprite palette slot sharing from a neutral plan (#1072) (#1080) (`5ee8ba24`)\n- NES: per-asset sprite palettes from the neutral palette plan (#1071) (#1079) (`f2125059`)\n- NES: background palettes from the neutral palette plan (#1070) (#1078) (`c7481870`)\n- Z80 family: injectable banking model with MBC1 for Game Boy (#1057) (#1074) (`d2ab6eec`)\n- Z80 family: shared builder and SM83/Z80 encoding dialects (#1056) (#1073) (`d10c7ead`)\n- Game Boy: palettes from the neutral palette plan (#1054) (#1069) (`3d7c9c43`)\n- Portable2D: neutral palette plan derived from art (#1053) (#1068) (`6543f6ab`)\n- Portable2D: color capabilities and ADR 0005 (#1052) (#1067) (`c3b343f4`)\n- SDK: neutral packed-camera slot schema (#1051) (#1066) (`8bbcbc68`)\n- Master System: target descriptor, capabilities, runtime memory layout and ABI (#1029) (#1064) (`2c850f49`)\n- Master System tooling: headless test machine and functional acceptance (#1028) (#1063) (`21b7b0d7`)\n- SDK: neutral camera stream plan (#1050) (#1062) (`1790d972`)\n- SDK: neutral camera streaming features (#1049) (#1061) (`73538530`)\n- SDK: neutral WorldPack runtime geometry and directory layout (#1048) (#1060) (`b371b0aa`)\n- ADR 0004: shared Z80-family codegen (#1027) (#1059) (`70a72e5f`)\n- GB: keep internal jump spans in one switchable bank (#1015) (#1047) (`4691d852`)\n- SDK: follow camera with static policy constants and one runtime (#1014) (#1045) (`435b8368`)\n- fix(gb): hide sprite draws skipped since the last publication (#1021) (#1043) (`8dac689c`)\n- Fix dotnet tool and standalone release packaging (#1042) (`654fb272`)\n- SDK collision: share the neutral AABB probe plan between Game Boy and NES (#925) (`da2310c5`)\n- fix(nes): keep small-world collision grids resident (#1020) (#1040) (`c2ee9372`)\n- Test: centralize Portable2D test-host package resolution (#1039) (`36b7349b`)\n- Fix NES running-jump camera stutter (#1022) (`51b799c5`)\n- feat(compiler): prune constant-selected branches at emission (#1019) (`57f3a06c`)\n- feat(sdk): configurable follow camera profiles (`28d6f7f6`)\n- docs: streamline agent guidance (`b05ba06b`)\n- fix: resume horizontal motion after clearing a wall (#1012) (`6e02d1be`)\n- sync: Update ROMs and sidecars (`1f617da3`)\n- feat: animate every runner-lift waterfall tile on GB and NES (`1d445fc2`)\n- feat(runner-lift): animate Part2 grass within NES video budget (#1010) (`d817bc1e`)\n- assets(runner-lift): prepare grass animation frames (#1009) (`02a6ee93`)\n- feat(runner-lift): update map collisions to use TSX Platform properties and regenerate ROMs (`4c905cc2`)\n- fix(runner-lift): optimize Part2 tileset to 30 unique tiles (tol 55) merging all duplicate groups (`303ff6a2`)\n- fix(runner-lift): optimize Part2 map (tolerance 40, GID 0 transparency, 46 unique tiles) (`fc9f0032`)\n- fix(runner-lift): optimize Part2 map tileset to 64 tiles using tolerance deduplication (`1b2873e9`)\n- feat: add portable kinematics source library (#1007) (`13c77107`)\n- research: evaluate portable kinematic controller (#993) (`6b5e04b6`)\n- fix(nes): keep fast WorldPack lookups for partial chunks (#1003) (`a868a862`)\n- test: freeze runner-lift scroll cadence replay (#1001) (`5455bd31`)\n- chore: balance Codex defaults and parallelize solution gate (#1000) (`f59e2315`)\n- feat: derive asset palettes and require PNG sprites (#996) (#999) (`e60687f4`)\n- Build: eliminar warnings del propio código y activar TreatWarningsAsErrors (#956) (#998) (`80cf9d15`)\n",
